# MDX Content Rules

## Required Frontmatter

```yaml
---
title: "Article Title"
slug: "article-slug"
date: "2026-01-22"  # Format: YYYY-MM-DD
description: "Brief description for SEO and cards"
readingTime: 15     # In minutes
category: "Blockchain"
tags: ["bitcoin", "blockchain", "cryptocurrency"]
featured: false
---
```

## Educational Components

Available components in MDX:

```markdown
<ConceptCard title="Key Concept">
  Explanation of important concept
</ConceptCard>

<BlockchainDiagram />
<TransactionFlow />
<NetworkDiagram />
<ProofOfWork />
<EthereumVsBitcoin />
<SmartContractFlow />
<DeFiEcosystem />
<ConsensusComparison />
<Layer2Comparison />
<DAOStructure />
<Web3Evolution />
<MiningVsStaking />
<SecurityVulnerabilities />
```

## Common MDX Issues

### Special Characters in Text

```markdown
❌ BAD - Causes parsing error
- Cheap electricity (<$0.05/kWh)

✅ GOOD - Use "less than" or escape
- Cheap electricity (less than $0.05/kWh)
```

### Component Imports

Components are auto-imported in `app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`:

```typescript
const mdxComponents = {
  ConceptCard,
  BlockchainDiagram,
  // ... all components
}
```

**New components must be:**
1. Created in `components/educational/`
2. Imported in `app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`
3. Added to `mdxComponents` object

### Image Paths

```markdown
✅ GOOD - Use web URLs or public folder
![Diagram](https://example.com/image.png)
![Diagram](/images/diagram.png)

❌ BAD - Relative paths don't work
![Diagram](./diagram.png)
```

## Multi-Language Content

Each article needs 3 files:
- `index.mdx` (English)
- `index.es.mdx` (Spanish)
- `index.zh-TW.mdx` (Traditional Chinese)

All must have identical structure and components.
